# armour/woman/scale: scale armour cut to the woman (ARMOUR-W, wave 2; STYLE_P2 25.2 / 25.3 / 27.4 and 14): the man's
# scale coat (armour/man/scale) on HER plate's cut: the waist a pixel in (the '-' cells), the shoulder caps under the
# pauldrons, the breast shaped by ONE step-1 row across the chest (the course under the first scales), no sculpting. Rows
# of 3 px scales, a lit top (step 3, a step-4 glint on the first scale) over a step-1 lower edge, the courses offset so
# they read as scallops; a steel gorget, her belt, a solid band hem over the fauld. Medium weight: the civilian silhouette
# plus the hang (scale_hang) and the shared pauldrons. Before this map her scale fell back to the mail hauberk.
# Finish regions: R the gorget's rim and the hem band, P the lit chest, G the chest socket, N the lowest course, W a 2x2
# spot on the shadow side. Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L (run / runl as her plate's).
# `sheen-dark,alloyshape` views: the antique sheen's flatter scales (lit tops a step down, the glint kept).
# Written by ARMOUR-W tools/mk_torso.py from src/torso_masters.txt (masters by hand). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body woman
role armour scale
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

